# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Data Science with R (AECN 896-05)
#
# The thing this file must NOT break: docs/ is the published site. GitHub Pages
# serves it. It is TRACKED, including its *_files/ asset directories.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Quarto / knitr intermediates ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scoped to the source tree so docs/**/*_files/ survives. /.quarto/ also holds
# a live deno-kv database that Dropbox creates conflicted copies of.
/.quarto/
/*_files/
/*_cache/
/lectures/**/*_files/
/lectures/**/*_cache/
/exercises/**/*_files/
/exercises/**/*_cache/
/syllabus/**/*_files/
/syllabus/**/*_cache/
/templates/**/*_files/
/templates/**/*_cache/

# ── Student work: never in a public repository ───────────────────────────────
# Student names and email addresses. The assignment sources themselves are
# tracked and published: _quarto.yml copies them into docs/ so students can
# download the .qmd they write their answers in.
/roster/

# ── Directories that are separate git repositories ───────────────────────────
# Tracking these would create broken gitlinks in the new repo.
/sample-project-reproducible/
/supplementary-material/
/data/

# ── Not part of the course site ──────────────────────────────────────────────
/sample-project/
/templates/
/Video/
/Datasets/
/FinalProject/
# Contains a business proposal, not course material.
# BOTH rules are needed. _quarto.yml does not exclude this from the render, so
# a full render keeps regenerating docs/IndustryPartnership/. Ignoring only the
# source would still publish the rendered proposal, because GitHub Pages serves
# whatever is committed under docs/.
/IndustryPartnership/
/docs/IndustryPartnership/

# ── Credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# L06 once carried a live USDA-NASS key that reached the public site.
.Renviron
.env
*.pem

# ── LaTeX byproducts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scoped to the source tree: docs/ may legitimately serve a .pdf or .tex.
/lectures/**/*.tex
/lectures/**/*.aux
/lectures/**/*.log
/exercises/**/*.tex
/syllabus/**/*.tex

# ── R / RStudio ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj

# ── Editor and OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
.vscode/
# Machine-specific paths; the rest of .claude/ is shared and tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Dropbox ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo lives in Dropbox, which leaves these behind after a sync race.
*conflicted copy*
.dropbox
.dropbox.attr

# ── Stray artefacts from running chunks interactively ────────────────────────
/a_list.rds
/_tmp-open.html

# ── Personal notes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*/chatGPT_questions.md

# Quarto writes these mid-render and deletes them at the end; they are not source.
*.rmarkdown

# ── Answer keys ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tracked on purpose, so a key is versioned with the assignment it answers.
# They are kept off the published site by _quarto.yml, which excludes
# *answer-key* from render: and never names one under resources:. This
# repository is public, so anyone who looks in it can read them.
